# Keep Wi-Fi associated across system suspend.
#
# cfg80211's wiphy_suspend() disconnects every interface of a phy that has no
# WoWLAN configuration (net/wireless/sysfs.c: cfg80211_leave_all). On LuneOS
# nothing ever set one - qcacld never does it itself and wpa_supplicant runs
# without a config file - so every suspend attempt tore the association down,
# the teardown took the driver's wakelocks, the kernel aborted the suspend,
# connman reassociated three seconds later and the next attempt hit the same
# wall: measured on sargo and tissot as a refused suspend every 30 s with a
# WiFi disconnect per attempt and never a successful sleep. With a WoWLAN
# trigger armed the association survives suspend and only the configured
# events wake the SoC.
#
# magic-packet is what every driver we ship advertises; "any" would keep the
# firmware waking the host on every frame. Which triggers a phone should arm
# (patterns for push notifications, for instance) is a policy question for
# later; this rule only stops the self-defeating disconnect.
SUBSYSTEM=="ieee80211", ACTION=="add", KERNEL=="phy*", RUN+="/usr/sbin/iw phy %k wowlan enable magic-packet"
